### Logical AND operator (`&&`) 
Another common shortcut you’ll encounter is the **or render nothing otherwise.** With `&&`, you could conditionally render the checkmark only if `isPacked` is `true`:
```


return (



  <li className="item">



    {name} {isPacked && '✅'}



  </li>




);


```

You can read this as _“if`isPacked` , then (`&&`) render the checkmark, otherwise, render nothing”_.
Here it is in action:
