`cache` lets you cache the result of a data fetch or computation.
```


const cachedFn = cache(fn);


```

  * [Reference ](https://18.react.dev/reference/react/cache#reference)
    * [`cache(fn)` ](https://18.react.dev/reference/react/cache#cache)
  * [Usage ](https://18.react.dev/reference/react/cache#usage)
    * [Cache an expensive computation ](https://18.react.dev/reference/react/cache#cache-expensive-computation)
    * [Share a snapshot of data ](https://18.react.dev/reference/react/cache#take-and-share-snapshot-of-data)
  * [Troubleshooting ](https://18.react.dev/reference/react/cache#troubleshooting)
